scope: "ComposeUX Peripheral HAL — a tiered hardware-abstraction model for binding physical peripherals to ComposeBus namespaces. A declarative sensor HAL covers the long tail of value/edge sensors (config-only, zero code); a reusable-driver tier covers standard bus-register parts; and a direct-integration escape covers stateful protocol devices. The generalization of the NFC/audio peripheral pattern ([CXC-NFC-PATTERN]). Captured 2026-07-10 (David)."
