**Version**: 0.1
**Created**: 2026-07-10
**Status**: CONCEPT CAPTURE (David 2026-07-10). Framing settled — tiered HAL (declarative value/edge sensors → reusable-driver bus parts → direct-integration stateful devices), the per-interaction-face boundary, define-once descriptor over per-platform drivers. Generalizes [CXC-NFC-PATTERN]; the input dual of the audio/display actuators. [CXC-HAL-OPEN] decisions need shaping before build. Natural fit with the embedded-reactive tier + the MinnowBoard lure sensors; not blocking Pass 4.

**[CXC-HAL-RELAY-ACTUATOR] ADDED — the Output Tier-1 declarative relay-bank actuator, hardware-verified (2026-08-05).** A sibling under [CXC-HAL-ACTUATE] capturing the shipped ESP32 4-relay fan controller: a `relay_actuator:` descriptor lowering a semantic ENUM namespace (`<device>/speed` = off|low|medium|high) to a bank of relays via a value→pin map, with a **break-before-make + dead-time MUST** (open ALL relays → wait `dead_time_ms` → close the single target; two speed relays never co-closed — motor safety; ~80 ms verified). Config-only, config-fetched on boot like every ESP32-class device and re-fetchable live ([CXC-ER-DEVICE]/[CXC-ER-REMOTE-RESTART]). Verified on a generic ESP32-WROOM-32E 4-relay board (active-HIGH; RY1=GPIO32 spare, RY2=GPIO33, RY3=GPIO25, RY4=GPIO26; low/med/high = RY2/RY3/RY4) by `office_fan` + `office_hepa` (identical board+firmware, differ only by id + namespace); firmware `firmware/reactive_core/src/relay_actuator.{h,cpp}`, host-tested in `env:native_test`. Compliance rows CXC-HAL-C1..C6 (the spec's first) + a new `## Relationships` block (REALIZES [CXC-HAL-ACTUATE]; RELATED_TO [CXC-ER-DEVICE] + [CXC-ER-REMOTE-RESTART]). **Architect: compliance numbering started at C1 (this spec had none — the "continue numbering" instruction had nothing to continue); a `## Relationships` section was added because this spec previously carried none (edges lived only in `part-of:` properties).**
